/**
 * @page architecture Operon architecture
 *
 * Operon is an in-process symbolic-regression library. Its architecture is
 * easiest to understand as three questions over a shared model: which
 * candidates come next, how good is one candidate, and what does its tree
 * compute. This page establishes those boundaries; the linked pages explain
 * their contracts and control flow.
 *
 * @section architecture-overview System overview
 *
 * Search owns candidate orchestration and consumes fitness. Evaluation turns
 * one candidate into fitness through its @c Evaluate then @c Score contract.
 * Execution computes sampled values, Jacobians, and static bounds without
 * knowing objectives or search. Coefficient fitting is deliberately separate:
 * it is an optional search-side collaborator that needs execution residuals and
 * Jacobians rather than objective scoring.
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph operon_overview {
 *   rankdir=TB;
 *   graph [bgcolor="transparent", pad=0.3, nodesep=0.6, ranksep=0.8];
 *   node [shape=box, style="rounded", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11, margin="0.14,0.1"];
 *   edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, color="#4a5568", fontcolor="#4a5568", arrowsize=0.7];
 *   entry [label="Entry points\noperon_gp | operon_nsgp | operon_enum", style="rounded,dashed"];
 *   search [label="Search\npopulation | variation | selection | reinsertion\nfitness cache | Taskflow orchestration"];
 *   evaluation [label="Evaluation\nEvaluate -> Score -> fitness\nmetrics | scaling | ErrMax | shape policy"];
 *   execution [label="Execution\ninterpreter / JIT: sampled execution\ninterval / affine: static bounds"];
 *   model [label="Model\nProblem | Dataset | PrimitiveSet\nIndividual | Tree"];
 *   fitting [label="Coefficient fitting\nLM | L-BFGS | SGD", style="rounded,dashed"];
 *   entry -> search [label="configures"];
 *   search -> evaluation [label="fitness of a candidate"];
 *   evaluation -> execution [label="values / bounds"];
 *   execution -> model;
 *   search -> fitting [label="optional local search", style=dashed];
 *   fitting -> execution [label="residuals / Jacobians"];
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 * @section architecture-pages System pages
 *
 * - @subpage core_model — shared formulation and representation vocabulary.
 * - @subpage execution — sampled execution, derivatives, JIT, and static
 *   bounds.
 * - @subpage evaluation — the @c Evaluate then @c Score objective contract.
 * - @subpage shape_constraints — optional static certification and enforcement.
 * - @subpage search_optimization — population-based search orchestration,
 *   local fitting, parallelism, and caches.
 * - @subpage grammar_enumeration — exhaustive grammar construction, fitting,
 *   and ranking without a population lifecycle.
 * - @subpage architecture_integration — CLI construction, serialization,
 *   reporting, and extension points.
 *
 * @section architecture-terms Vocabulary
 *
 * | Term | Meaning |
 * | --- | --- |
 * | Candidate / individual | An @c Individual: a tree genotype plus fitness. |
 * | Sampled execution | Running a tree over dataset rows. |
 * | Bound | Static interval or affine analysis over a domain box. |
 * | Evaluate | The evaluator phase that may produce an @c EvaluatedBuffer. |
 * | Score | The evaluator phase that converts an evaluation result into fitness. |
 * | Fit | Coefficient optimization; distinct from linear scaling and scoring. |
 * | Feasible | Certified to meet shape constraints over its configured domain. |
 */
